{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSwvMuoFj63XHqh7QqNJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the full reading before I draw anything. I haven't written to the board.\n\n**Question:** which statuses can a Roamstay booking have, and what moves it between them?\n**Outcome:** the product, engineering and support team agree every status and its exits before the next story is written.\n\n**What each source settled**\n* Your request gives the 7 states, the moves and who triggers them: the guest cancels, the hotel marks No-show, and the card authorisation confirms.\n* The board read gave the destination. It is a new section named \"Booking status\" beside Sprint retro, which stays untouched.\n* Your two recommended-answer replies settled the reader, the \"must not\" list, the \"check in\" trigger and an unguarded cancel from Confirmed.\n\n**Outline, in drawing order**\n1. Start, then Pending.\n2. Pending to Confirmed, labelled \"card authorised\".\n3. Inside Confirmed: start, then Upcoming. Upcoming to In stay, labelled \"check in\".\n4. Confirmed to Completed, labelled \"check out [from In stay]\".\n5. Pending to Cancelled and Confirmed to Cancelled, both labelled \"guest cancels\".\n6. Confirmed to No-show, labelled \"missed check-in [from Upcoming]\".\n7. Completed, Cancelled and No-show each go to an end dot.\n\nThat is 7 states and 12 transitions, all of them labelled except the start and end arrows. I found nothing to cut, since each state and move comes from your lines.\n\n**Two framings**\n* A full state map, with every status and every exit visible. It costs three end states on the right.\n* A happy path only, with cancellation and No-show left to a table. It is quieter, but it hides the exits you asked for.\n* Recommended: the full state map, because you named both exits.\n\n**The look**\n* First glance: Pending, the light blue start state, since your request names no state to stress.\n* Zone: Confirmed is the only zone, drawn around Upcoming and In stay.\n* Title: \"Booking status\".\n* Subtitle: \"Every status a Roamstay booking passes through, and what moves it on\".\n* Source line: \"Source: the booking lifecycle as described by the product owner. Left out: declined-card and expiry paths.\"\n* Detail balanced, audience mixed, laptop reading distance.\n\n**Assumed, and what would settle each**\n* Cancelled and No-show end the booking. A line from you would settle it.\n* No-show leaves from Upcoming only. Tell me if the hotel can also mark it from another status.\n* Your lines are current behavior. A source doc would settle it.\n* A guest can cancel mid-stay, since the move leaves Confirmed with no guard. Tell me if cancelling is only possible before check-in.\n* The detail, audience and distance settings above.\n\n**Still open:** nothing is unasked.\n\nIs this the right reading of the board?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1343,"cache_read_input_tokens":100932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1343},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb60273d-f575-4523-880d-c6a86b55310a","uuid":"a7cd89ea-545d-4ac9-a678-6adf7abba5f2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T15:05:17.275Z","request_id":"req_011CgSwvMYE4V1Ax75GKeqr4"}
